Sure did.

353
00:15:11,350 --> 00:15:13,530
我本该摔门而去
Well, I would storm out of here,

354
00:15:13,530 --> 00:15:15,680
但手套和钢丝刷已经在我手里了
but I already have the gloves and the steel wool,

355
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,990
我本来也很喜欢清理烤箱  快让开
and I really do love cleaning an oven. Move.

356
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:22,140
她拐我做了所有的家务
She made me do all her chores,

357
00:15:22,140 --> 00:15:23,560
这还不是她的原创
and it wasn't even her idea--

358
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:26,800
是偷《汤姆·索亚历险记》里的招数
she stole it from Tom Sawyer.

359
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,100
得了吧  别发神经了
You know what? This is crazy.

360
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:30,760
人家霍华德和艾米是一起工作  别乱想了
Howard and Amy are working together-- get over it.

361
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,000
莱纳德  你干什么呢
Leonard, what are you doing?

362
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:32,970
"必要时得喊停"
"Knowing when to say when."

363
00:15:32,970 --> 00:15:34,340
这不是什么大事
This is not a big deal.

364
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:35,590
这是一件大事
It is a big deal.

365
00:15:35,590 --> 00:15:38,790
霍华德让艾米习惯了欢笑和音乐
Howard's getting Amy used to laughing and listening to music.

366
00:15:38,790 --> 00:15:41,230
万一她回家也想玩这么疯呢
What if she expects that madness at home?

367
00:15:41,230 --> 00:15:42,750
你说得有道理
Yeah, that is a good point.

368
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:45,200
你能把自己的感受说出来  我为你骄傲
I'm really proud of the way you're able to express your feelings.

369
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:47,270
谢谢  我只是太生气了
Thank you. I'm just so angry.

370
00:15:47,330 --> 00:15:49,730
你知道  每个人都会生气的
You know, everyone gets angry.

371
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:53,710
所有的爸比们和妈咪们也会生气
Even mommies and daddies.

372
00:15:54,750 --> 00:15:57,670
你不会觉得现在应该"肯定他的行为"吧
You can't think this is the right time to "Validate his behavior."

373
00:15:57,670 --> 00:15:59,840
那我们试试"父母统一战线"如何
Okay, what about "Presenting a united front"?

374
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:02,270
不如试试你溺爱他  让他永远无法成长吧
What about you coddling him and he's never gonna learn?

375
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:03,180
听着
Look.

376
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:07,160
你听起来很生气  我觉得你能够
You sound frustrated, and I'm really proud of the way

377
00:16:07,170 --> 00:16:09,950
把自己的想法说出来  非常棒
you're able to state your opinion.

378
00:16:11,290 --> 00:16:11,980
谢谢
Thank you.

379
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:13,360
等一下  不对
Wait, no, no.

380
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:16,770
你别用书上的东西对付我
Don't use that book on me.

381
00:16:16,770 --> 00:16:18,440
等一下  什么书
W-Wait, what book?

382
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:21,560
佩妮一直在用博纳黛特的育儿书对付你
Penny's been using one of Bernadette's parenting books on you.

383
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,480
什么  他还不是一样
What? So has he.

384
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:27,670
你们凭什么把我当小孩对待
Wh-What makes you think you can treat me like a child?

385
00:16:30,270 --> 00:16:33,630
你用的是芝麻街大鸟形状的洗发水
Your shampoo comes in a Big Bird bottle.

386
00:16:33,630 --> 00:16:37,320
那是因为成人洗发水会辣到我的爷们眼睛
That's because the adult shampoo burns my man eyes.

387
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:42,140
你在忙什么呢
Hey, what are you working on?

388
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:44,150
我的天  你还在呢
Oh, my God, you're still here?

389
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:47,970
我当然还在啦
Well, of course I'm here.

390
00:16:47,970 --> 00:16:49,850
我能理解你的感受
I know what you're going through.

391
00:16:49,850 --> 00:16:54,370
真的吗  你家也有一个缺爱的印度人吗
Really? You have a needy Indian man in your house?

392
00:16:54,970 --> 00:16:58,400
本来是有的  后来他到你家来了
I did, but then he came over here.

393
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:01,110
这就是咱们有孩子之后的模样吗
So is this how it's gonna be if we have kids?

394
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:02,660
你就这样把一切怪在我的头上
You're just gonna throw me under the bus?

395
00:17:02,660 --> 00:17:04,810
如果你用溺爱谢尔顿的方式教他们  那就会
If you spoil them the way you do Sheldon, then, yeah.

396
00:17:04,810 --> 00:17:06,240
我的办法很有用好嘛
Uh, my way was working.

397
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:07,510
我觉得你生气
Okay? I think you're just upset

398
00:17:07,510 --> 00:17:09,640
是因为在某些方面你跟我没得比
because there are some things I am better than you at.

399
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,590
你不能把介词放在句子的结尾
Well, you can't end a sentence with a preposition,

400
00:17:11,590 --> 00:17:14,040
所以你比我厉害的肯定不是语法
so clearly, not grammar.

401
00:17:14,560 --> 00:17:16,480
你这么聪明  你猜你这句话聪不聪明
If you're so smart, was that a smart thing to say?

402
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:17,670
看情况  在我回答之前
That depends. Before I said it,

403
00:17:17,670 --> 00:17:19,110
咱俩今晚的滚床单还有戏吗
was sex tonight still on the table?

404
00:17:19,120 --> 00:17:21,020
-没戏了  -那我说的话没毛病
- No. - Then it's fine.

405
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:25,720
一旦我们能让它运作起来
You know, once we get this operational,

406
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:28,330
我们就有可能实现无线化操作了
we could probably figure out how to make it wireless.

407
00:17:28,330 --> 00:17:30,200
那就太棒了
That'd be amazing.

408
00:17:31,290 --> 00:17:33,100
谢尔顿发信息来了
Oh, that's Sheldon.

409
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:36,150
他在生莱纳德和佩妮的气
Oh, he's upset with Leonard and Penny.

410
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:38,800
还有博纳黛特
And Bernadette.

411
00:17:40,210 --> 00:17:41,840
还有马克·吐温
And Mark Twain.

412
00:17:44,810 --> 00:17:46,470
博纳黛特之前也发来了信息
Yeah, Bernadette texted earlier.

413
00:17:46,470 --> 00:17:48,490
拉杰快把她逼疯了
Raj is really getting on her nerves.

414
00:17:48,590 --> 00:17:51,490
最近咱俩的确加班有些多
Well, I guess we have been working late a lot.

415
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:53,820
我们要不现在收工回家吧
Should we call it a night and go home?

416
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:57,320
我们也可以煮壶咖啡  继续攀登科学的高峰
Or we could brew a pot of coffee and power through.

417
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:59,480
是吗  现在都这么晚了
I don't know, it's getting kind of late.

418
00:18:00,170 --> 00:18:01,830
我的表哪里去了
Hey, where's my watch?

419
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:05,040
去问问你的骷髅吧
Why don't you ask your skeleton?

420
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:12,970
我的妈呀  你是怎么办到的
Oh, my God. How is that even possible?!

421
00:18:19,310 --> 00:18:21,470
我们俩一起玩  这真是极好的
This is great, the two of us hanging out.

422
00:18:21,470 --> 00:18:22,860
之前怎么没想到呢
Why didn't we think of this earlier?

423
00:18:22,860 --> 00:18:23,750
同意
Agreed.

424
00:18:23,750 --> 00:18:25,930
我不需要和艾米一起看电影
I don't need Amy to watch a movie.

425
00:18:25,930 --> 00:18:28,630
我也能轻松地不牵你手
I can not hold your hand just as easily.

426
00:18:33,750 --> 00:18:39,300
在原著中  这个男的就是杀手
In the book this is based on, that man's the killer.

